# Flutter & Dart Conventions

## Dart Style

- Prefer `const` constructors wherever possible
- Use `final` for fields that don't change after initialization
- Use named parameters for widgets with more than 2 parameters
- Follow effective Dart naming: `lowerCamelCase` for variables/functions, `UpperCamelCase` for classes/enums

## Widget Patterns

- Prefer `StatelessWidget` over `StatefulWidget` unless local mutable state is needed
- Use `FutureBuilder` for loading async data in widgets
- Extract private helper widgets as `_WidgetName` in the same file for page-specific components
- All pages use plain `Scaffold` (not AppScaffold -- that's deprecated)

## Theming

- Never hardcode colors -- always use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme`
- Tajweed colours are standalone constants in `lib/ui/widgets/tajweed.dart` (e.g. `kQalqalaColor`, `kGhunnahColor`) used by the Tajweed Guide. The reader uses only V4 font-based tajweed.
- Font sizes for Arabic/English are user-configurable via `SettingsScope.of(context)`

## Arabic Text

- Always use the `ArabicText` widget for rendering Arabic content (handles font, RTL, OpenType features; set `v4FontFamily` for V4 tajweed in the reader)
- Do not use raw `Text` widgets for Arabic strings
- **Never strip diacritics** from Quran Arabic text -- they are essential for correct recitation
- Use `aya_text` (Uthmani) for display; use `aya_text_emlaey` only for search indexing
- Tajweed coloring applies ONLY to Quran text, not Hadith Arabic
- Never truncate Arabic text mid-word -- always break at word boundaries

## Navigation

- Use go_router: `context.push('/path')` for pushing, `context.go('/path')` for tab switching
- Route definitions are in `lib/router.dart`
- Bottom nav tabs: Home (`/home`), Quran (`/quran`), Hadith (`/hadith`), Bookmarks (`/bookmarks`), Settings (`/settings`)
- Detail pages push above the shell (no bottom nav): `/quran/:surahId`, `/hadith/:collection/:book`, `/search`

## Data Access

- Use repository classes to load data from assets -- never call `rootBundle` directly in widgets
- Asset paths are centralized in the `AssetPaths` class (`lib/data/asset_paths.dart`)

## Bookmarks

- Access via `BookmarkScope.of(context)` -- provides `BookmarkService`
- Bookmark IDs: `quran:{surahId}:{ayah}` or `hadith:{collection}:{book}:{index}`
- Use `service.toggleBookmark(...)` to add/remove
- Use `service.isBookmarked(id)` to check state
